# GitHub profile README — daily sync

Profile draft lives at `docs/github-profile-README.md` (append-only vs live `lilaclilac09/lilaclilac09`).

## Automation

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/github-profile-readme-sync.yml` — cron `0 10 * * *` UTC + `workflow_dispatch`
- Script: `node scripts/sync-github-profile-readme.mjs` (rewrites marker blocks from last 14d merged PRs)
- Optional secret `PROFILE_README_TOKEN`: PAT with `contents:write` on `lilaclilac09/lilaclilac09` to push the live profile README

## When an agent touches this

1. After meaningful merges (Console / polar-lab / Cafe Cursor / memory), run `node scripts/sync-github-profile-readme.mjs` and commit if changed.
2. Do **not** rewrite Featured Dispatch / Research & Builds / Process & Precision unless the user asks — only refresh marked Recently* sections (or append bullets).
3. English only; match `**Name**: prose` style.
4. Live profile push still needs `PROFILE_README_TOKEN` or App install on `lilaclilac09/lilaclilac09` — without it, update the draft + tell the user to paste.
